d Public Health Committee","date":"14/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"ECET 2026-27 Budget Monitoring Quarter 1","url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk/documents/s50144740/ecet-2026-27-budget-monitoring-quarter-1.pdf","committee":"Environment, Climate Emergency and Transport Committee","date":"08/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"Carbon Budget Performance Report 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk/documents/s50144357/carbon-budget-performance-report-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Environment, Climate Emergency and Transport Committee","date":"08/07/2026","key":false},{"title":"Appendix 1 - Carbon Budget Performance 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk/documents/s50144358/appendix-1-carbon-budget-performance-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Environment, Climate Emergency and Transport Committee","date":"08/07/2026","key":false}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-12","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed; Council Reserve","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-27","committee":"Audit and Risk Management Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-30","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed; Council Reserve","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-07","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-20","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Cancelled; Council Reserve","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Policy and Resources Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Pensions Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wirral.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Wirral pension fund budget jumps 57% as new investment company launches","lead":"The Merseyside Pension Fund's administration budget will rise to \u00a338.5m in 2026/27, up from \u00a324.5m in the previous year, the Pensions Committee heard today. The \u00a314m increase is primarily driven by set-up costs and management fees for Northern LGPS, a new FCA-regulated investment company managing pension schemes across the Northern authorities. The committee also authorized the Director of Pensions to provide regulatory capital for Northern LGPS as determined by the Financial Conduct Authority's requirements. In separate audit findings, Grant Thornton expects to give the fund an unqualified opinion on its 2025/26 accounts, though a prior-year recommendation to implement monitoring of the Oracle Fusion financial system for unauthorized activity remains in progress.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"LOCAL GOVERNMENT PENSION SCHEME (LGPS) PENSIONS DASHBOARDS ECOSYSTEM: POST-CONNECTION WORKSTREAM","paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146243/50146243.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Local Pension Board","paper_title":"26Sept MPF AR&amp;A 2025-26 App 1","paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146629/50146629.pdf","headline":"Fund investment performance in 2025/26 exceeded forecast by \u00a3929 million, with total assets rising to \u00a312.2 billion.","detail":"Fund assets increased from \u00a310.96 billion to \u00a312.19 billion. This significantly exceeded the forecast gain of \u00a3299.6 million, representing a \u00a3929 million variance. The fund achieved 13.5% investment return against a benchmark of 13.6%, showing close alignment with strategy and effective management.","category":"other","matters":"Better-than-forecast investment returns reduce pressure for future contribution increases and demonstrate effective asset management, supporting the long-term sustainability of pension obligations and employer costs.","figures":"Fund value growth: \u00a31,228,679k; variance to forecast: \u00a3929,090k; investment return 13.5% vs benchmark 13.6%","quote":"The value of the Fund increased by \u00a31.2 billion from \u00a311 billion at 31 March 2025 to \u00a312.2 billion at 31 March 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Local Pension Board","paper_title":"26Sept MPF AR&amp;A 2025-26 App 1","paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146629/50146629.pdf","headline":"Pension fund actuarial valuation improves to 116% funded, allowing employer contribution rate to fall from 18.5% to 16.2%.","detail":"The triennial actuarial valuation completed in December 2025 showed the fund's funding position improving from 106% to 116% of its liabilities. As a consequence, the average employer contribution rate for future service was reduced by 2.3 percentage points. Wirral Council, as the administering authority and a significant employer, will benefit from lower required pension contributions, improving its budget position.","category":"other","matters":"A reduction in the council's pension contribution burden directly improves its revenue budget and reduces future cost pressures, affecting the council's financial resilience and ability to meet other obligations.","figures":"Funding level improved from 106% to 116%; employer contribution rate reduced from 18.5% to 16.2%","quote":"As a consequence, and following consultation, we were able to reduce the average employer future service contribution rate from 18.5% to 16.2%.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Local Pension Board","paper_title":"LOCAL GOVERNMENT PENSION SCHEME (LGPS) PENSIONS DASHBOARDS ECOSYSTEM: POST-CONNECTION WORKSTREAM","paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146297/50146297.pdf","headline":"AVC data reconciliation involves complex matching challenges from multiple provider approaches and data inconsistencies","detail":"Section 3.7 identifies AVCs as particularly complex for dashboard implementation due to matching problems from differences in personal data, member identifiers and historic records. Section 3.8-3.9 notes the Fund's AVC providers use different approaches (direct to dashboard vs via administering authority), each carrying different operational and governance implications.","category":"governance","matters":"AVC data quality and reconciliation issues could impede dashboard compliance and create exposure to accuracy claims.","figures":"None provided","quote":"The wider LGPS community has recognised that AVCs are a particularly complex aspect of dashboard implementation with regard to reconciliation and consistent matching of AVC records with main scheme records as differences in personal data, member identifiers and historic records can lead to matching problems.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Local Pension Board","paper_title":"LOCAL GOVERNMENT PENSION SCHEME (LGPS) PENSIONS DASHBOARDS ECOSYSTEM: POST-CONNECTION WORKSTREAM","paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146297/50146297.pdf","headline":"Regulatory non-compliance could trigger regulatory intervention, remediation costs and member compensation claims","detail":"Section 7.1 warns that failure to meet dashboard obligations could lead to regulatory intervention, remediation costs, reputational damage and emergency corrective work. Section 7.2 notes inaccurate data could expose the fund to maladministration complaints and compensation claims. Section 5.2 frames non-compliance as breach of legal duty, not service failure.","category":"audit","matters":"Unbudgeted regulatory costs and compensation liabilities could hit fund finances; compliance failures damage credibility and member confidence.","figures":"None provided","quote":"Failure to meet dashboard obligations could lead to regulatory intervention, remediation costs, reputational damage and emergency corrective work.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Local Pension Board","paper_title":"LOCAL GOVERNMENT PENSION SCHEME (LGPS) PENSIONS DASHBOARDS ECOSYSTEM: POST-CONNECTION WORKSTREAM","paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146297/50146297.pdf","headline":"Resource requirements for dashboards cannot be quantified because actual member demand remains unknown","detail":"Section 6.1 acknowledges that while increased member engagement is anticipated at 2027/28 launch, actual demand is unforecast. Section 6.4 warns that incomplete member data could drive significant additional resource requirements. Section 6.5 notes officers are still assessing what resources may be needed.","category":"demand","matters":"Cost impacts cannot be fully quantified; high member demand could materially exceed resource projections.","figures":"None provided","quote":"as actual demand levels remain unknown, monitoring activity levels will assist in understanding emerging usage patterns.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Wirral","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Fund investment performance in 2025/26 exceeded forecast by \u00a3929 million, with total assets rising to \u00a312.2 billion.","lead":"Better-than-forecast investment returns reduce pressure for future contribution increases and demonstrate effective asset management, supporting the long-term sustainability of pension obligations and employer costs.","also":["32 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Policy and Resources Committee on 2026-10-21","n_findings":33,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"26Sept MPF AR&amp;A 2025-26 App 1","top_paper_url":"https://wirral.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50146629/50146629.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":93,"news_drafts_total":1}}